---
title: Starting phases
description: "Phase packs: a starting phase for programs, like Find your weights, with the block, progression and questions it comes with, under one listing and one install."
---

A starting phase is the first weeks of a program that does something different, like LogIt's
**Find your weights**: a week that works up to a hard set on each lift, so the program after it
starts from real numbers. A coach adds one in the program builder with **+ Phase**; it brings its
weeks, the block that runs each lift in them, and a progression for them.

A phase pack is data only. The parts it uses are ordinary plugins, listed in `includes` and
installed with it: a [workout block](/docs/plugins/workout-blocks), a
[progression](/docs/plugins/progression) and a question pack. Coaches find phase packs under
Coaching › Plugins › Starting phases.

## phase.json

```json
{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "id": "app.getlogit.find-your-weights",
  "name": "Find your weights",
  "description": "A first week that works up to a hard set on each lift.",
  "phase": { "name": "Find your weights", "weeks": 1, "findsWeights": true, "block": "app.getlogit.weight-finder" },
  "includes": ["app.getlogit.weight-finder"]
}
```

- `phase.weeks`: how long it usually runs, 1 to 12. The coach can change it.
- `phase.findsWeights`: it works up to the weights that fit. Its weeks become "Find your weights"
  weeks; when it ends the coach checks what it found on Today, and the next phase plans from it.
- `phase.block`: a workout block that runs each lift in the phase's weeks. Its field of type
  `exercise` is set to the lift. Give the block `countsAs.sets` so each entry is a real set of the
  lift; history, estimates and records then see it like any other set.
- `phase.progression`: a progression for the phase's weeks. It's told the week (`input.week`) and
  where each estimate came from (`input.estimate`).
- `includes`: the plugins installed with the pack, up to 6. Anything `block` or `progression`
  names has to be here.

## The Weight finder block

LogIt's own Find your weights runs this block. Each entry is a jump; "how many more could you have
done?" is reps in reserve, so 2 more is RPE 8.

```json
{
  "id": "app.getlogit.weight-finder",
  "name": "Weight finder",
  "entry": { "one": "Jump", "many": "Jumps" },
  "blockFields": [{ "key": "lift", "type": "exercise", "label": "Lift" }],
  "fields": [
    { "key": "kg", "type": "weight", "label": "kg", "column": true },
    { "key": "reps", "type": "number", "label": "Reps", "default": 6, "column": true },
    { "key": "left", "type": "choice", "label": "How many more could you have done?", "options": ["0", "1", "2", "3", "4+"], "column": true }
  ],
  "countsAs": { "sets": { "exercise": "lift", "weight": "kg", "reps": "reps", "rir": "left" } }
}
```

## On the client's phone

A block from a pack runs code only if its parts do. LogIt's own blocks (`app.getlogit.`) are data
and come with the program; other plugins are allowed by the client once, like any plugin a coach's
program uses. Without the block on their phone, the lift runs as a normal exercise with a note on
what to do.
